    <h1 class="h-xl" tabindex="-1" data-focus>We had to figure it out alone. They shouldn’t have to.</h1>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="sec tight"><div class="wrap split">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Own Two Feet started with three students, Dane, Jewell and Marco, comparing notes. We’d all been the person people turned to for a frozen laptop, a cabinet off its hinge, a wall that needed paint, or a car that wouldn’t start. Most of the time, nobody had shown us how.</p>
      <p>Some of us grew up without a dad around much. All of us watched parents and relatives work long hours to keep things going. <strong>A busy parent isn’t a missing parent.</strong> Sometimes everyone’s just busy, and a kid steps up and figures it out alone.</p>
      <p>So we asked a simple question: how many other boys are in the same spot? The problem isn’t that they can’t learn. It’s that someone may never have had the time to teach them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel sage" style="padding:clamp(26px,3vw,40px);display:grid;gap:14px"><h2 class="h-md">Still building</h2><p class="muted">Own Two Feet is a student venture. We’re writing our workshops now, and seven free topic manuals are ready to read. No workshops are running yet, and we’re not booking any.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:6px"><a class="btn btn-ink btn-sm" href="#interest">Join the Interest List</a><a class="btn btn-line btn-sm" href="manuals/">See the Manuals</a></div></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="sec tight"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="h-lg">Who we are</h2><p class="lede">Three Baylor University students on one venture team. We run the interviews, write the workshops and build this site ourselves.</p></div>
    <div class="team">
      <article class="member"><div class="photo"><span>Photo coming</span></div><h3>Marco Melchor</h3><p class="role">Mechanical engineering, Baylor University, graduating December 2027</p><p>Two engineering internships at Halliburton. Co-founder and Vice President of Baylor’s SHPE chapter, and President of the Engineering and Computer Science Dean’s Committee. He built this site and the activities, and his mom’s words are the first quote on the home page.</p></article>
      <article class="member"><div class="photo"><span>Photo coming</span></div><h3>Dane</h3><p class="role">Interviews and research, Baylor University</p><p>Dane started with the people closest to him, his own father and an uncle, then friends like Jayden S. The same thing came up every time: they wished someone had shown them when they were younger. Those conversations are a big part of why we started.</p></article>
      <article class="member"><div class="photo"><span>Photo coming</span></div><h3>Jewell</h3><p class="role">Interviews and customer research, Baylor University</p><p>Jewell talked to five people, from Shepherd S. at 14 to adults looking back on growing up without much help at home. Joseph P.’s line about videos not being a relationship is why every workshop is hands-on. Jewell’s interview with Steven S. is what pointed us toward schools and community groups as the ones who bring workshops to students.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="wrap"><div class="panel sand">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="h-lg">Our interviews shaped the plan</h2><p class="lede" style="color:#46504A">We talked to parents, mentors and young men about growing up and learning this stuff.</p></div>
    <div class="stg values hscroll" id="ivRow">
      <div class="value"><h3>Videos help, but they don’t stick</h3><p>Stuff you learn alone from a video is easy to forget. Learning from a real person sticks.</p></div>
      <div class="value"><h3>Kids don’t want to bother busy parents</h3><p>A lot of boys figure things out on their own so they don’t add to their parents’ stress.</p></div>
      <div class="value"><h3>Asking for help is hard</h3><p>Workshops have to make questions feel normal and safe.</p></div>
      <div class="value"><h3>Not everyone thinks they need it</h3><p>So we focus on what free videos can’t give you: hands-on practice with someone there to help.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="rowctl"><button class="icon-btn" type="button" id="ivPrev" aria-label="Previous interview finding"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 6l-6 6 6 6"/></svg></button><button class="icon-btn" type="button" id="ivNext" aria-label="Next interview finding"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></button><span class="count" id="ivCount" aria-live="polite">1 of 4</span></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="sec tight"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="h-lg">Four commitments</h2></div>
    <div class="stg values commit" id="commits">
      <details class="value tint-1" open><summary><h3>Support families, never replace them</h3></summary><p>We work alongside parents, counselors and mentors, and send skills home with students.</p></details>
      <details class="value tint-2" open><summary><h3>Practice beats watching</h3></summary><p>Students learn by doing, with someone nearby to answer questions and catch mistakes.</p></details>
      <details class="value tint-3" open><summary><h3>Know your limits</h3></summary><p>Knowing when to stop and ask for help is a skill too, and we teach it every session.</p></details>
      <details class="value tint-4" open><summary><h3>Confidence, not judgment</h3></summary><p>No student is behind because of how his family works. Everyone starts somewhere.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div></section>
